    "forensics": "The losing cluster is primarily driven by tight stop-loss whipsaws (0.55% SL) during post-morning consolidation (10:25\u201311:10 IST), where normal 5-minute mean-reverting noise prematurely triggers exits (e.g., TATASTEEL stopped out within 5 minutes on Oct 21). Additionally, repeated entries in low-momentum regimes (such as two consecutive losses in TATASTEEL on Oct 22) and EOD square-offs with tiny gross gains highlight severe fee drag (\u20b933.11 fees vs \u20b98.68 net P&L) caused by insufficient institutional volume filtering and delayed breakeven protection.",
    "learning": "In Indian NSE large-cap cash equities, intraday liquidity sweeps after the initial opening hour require higher volume thresholds (>2.4x) to filter retail head-fakes, wider structural stop-losses (~0.65%) to survive normal bid-ask and 5-minute bar noise, and faster breakeven triggers (1.0R) to neutralize statutory transaction costs and brokerage drag on small-capital accounts.",
